cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this skill in your research or tooling, please cite it as below."
title: "mri-research: A Claude skill for MRI reconstruction research"
abstract: >-
  A curated, verified reference-hub skill for Claude that provides fluent
  orientation across the magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) reconstruction
  research ecosystem: MR physics and k-space foundations, landmark
  reconstruction methods (parallel imaging, compressed sensing, low-rank,
  deep learning, and diffusion/score-based recon), software toolboxes, raw-data
  formats and open datasets, pulse-sequence and trajectory design, MRI
  hardware, and programmatic literature access. It points to the community's
  primary resources rather than bundling datasets or copyrighted text.
type: software
